<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>items</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>Read from the tweak running inside the Bluetooth daemon. "No data yet" means the tweak has not written anything: it is not loaded, or the daemon's sandbox blocks every log channel.</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Status</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSTitleValueCell</string>
			<key>get</key>
			<string>loadedValue:</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Loaded in daemon</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSTitleValueCell</string>
			<key>get</key>
			<string>lastEventValue:</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Last event</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSTitleValueCell</string>
			<key>get</key>
			<string>channelValue:</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Log channels</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Debug log</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>action</key>
			<string>showLog:</string>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSButtonCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>View debug log</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>action</key>
			<string>copyLog:</string>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSButtonCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Copy log to clipboard</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>action</key>
			<string>clearLog:</string>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSButtonCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Clear log</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>The v7.7 Sink trial returned 0x68 and is retired. v7.8 only reads endpoint occupancy. Legacy Sink is inactive. Live reception and SDP 0x110B are not implemented.</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Experiments</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSSwitchCell</string>
			<key>default</key>
			<false/>
			<key>defaults</key>
			<string>com.apple.bluetooth</string>
			<key>key</key>
			<string>BTPhonoSinkExperiments</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Legacy sink experiment flag (inactive)</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>OFF by default. When ON, the next bluetoothd launch adds an experimental read-only observer for existing SDP record additions. It never adds Sink services or endpoints. Restart bluetoothd once after changing. Switch OFF and restart if instability occurs.</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Optional SDP registration diagnostics</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSSwitchCell</string>
			<key>default</key>
			<false/>
			<key>defaults</key>
			<string>com.apple.bluetooth</string>
			<key>key</key>
			<string>BTPhonoSinkSDPProbe</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Trace existing SDP records (advanced)</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>v8.0 init lookup observation</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>OFF by default. Advanced test: installs an additional pass-through hook on the private AVDTP config getter on the next bluetoothd launch. Never changes its result or allocates endpoints. Only enable after confirming headphone playback; disable and restart if Bluetooth becomes unstable.</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSSwitchCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Trace AVDTP config lookup (advanced)</string>
			<key>defaults</key>
			<string>com.apple.bluetooth</string>
			<key>key</key>
			<string>BTPhonoSinkV80ConfigLookupObserver</string>
			<key>default</key>
			<false/>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>v8.1: One-time capacity test</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>Advanced, potentially disruptive. Default OFF. If armed, next bluetoothd restart consumes this switch before attempting to change AVDTP initializer count from 6 to 7 using a persistent shadow config. NO Sink endpoint is registered. Verify headphone behavior and export log, then check switch reset OFF. Recovery: turn OFF and restart daemon or reinstall v8.0.</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSSwitchCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Arm seven slots for ONE restart</string>
			<key>defaults</key>
			<string>com.apple.bluetooth</string>
			<key>key</key>
			<string>BTPhonoSinkV81SevenOnce</string>
			<key>default</key>
			<false/>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key><string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>label</key><string>v8.8 continuous audio experiment</string>
			<key>footerText</key><string>One-restart private-stack test. Requires BOTH this switch and seven-slot one-shot ON before restart. v8.8 forwards SBC to a separate audio helper after START is accepted. Both switches reset OFF before changes. Test at moderate volume; export the debug log and restart Bluetooth with switches OFF to end the trial.</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key><string>PSSwitchCell</string>
			<key>label</key><string>Arm real Sink SDP + signaling ONCE</string>
			<key>defaults</key><string>com.apple.bluetooth</string>
			<key>key</key><string>BTPhonoSinkV82DecisiveOnce</string>
			<key>default</key><false/>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>title</key>
	<string>BTPhonoSink</string>
</dict>
</plist>
